# Task #72. `ignored` never uses its parameter, so the write it is handed is
# never forced, and laziness means an effect never forced is an effect that
# never happens. The program prints "dropped it" and writes nothing, on both
# engines, with no diagnostic.
#
# The language's stated position is the opposite: a function whose body does
# io must hand the io back, or it "would abandon the effects above it". That
# check reads a function's own body, so an effect abandoned inside somebody
# else's parameter walks past it.
import "std/io"

fn ignored _
  "dropped it"

pub play =
  r = ignored (io/write "this write never happens\n")
  print r
